I'd be happy to! 

Think of standard deviation simply as a measure of **spread**. It tells us how far away the numbers in a list are from their mean (average). 

Here is a quick example using three different sets of numbers that all have the exact same mean (10):

*   **Set 1:** {10, 10, 10} 
    *   The mean is 10. Every single number is exactly 10, so there is zero spread. The standard deviation is **0**.
*   **Set 2:** {9, 10, 11}
    *   The mean is 10. The numbers are very close to the mean, so the standard deviation is **small**.
*   **Set 3:** {1, 10, 19}
